<article class="env-lemma" id="0946">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0946">Lemma <span data-tag="0946">21.51.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $U$ be a weakly contractible object of $\mathcal{C}$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the functor $\mathcal{F} \mapsto \mathcal{F}(U)$ is an exact functor $\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C}) \to \textit{Ab}$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^ p(U, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for every abelian sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ and all $p \geq 1$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for any sheaf of groups $\mathcal{G}$ any $\mathcal{G}$-torsor has a section over $U$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The first statement follows immediately from the definition (see also Homology, Section <a href="/tag/010M" data-tag="010M">12.7</a>). The higher derived functors vanish by Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015F" data-tag="015F">13.16.9</a>. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a $\mathcal{G}$-torsor. Then $\mathcal{F} \to *$ is a surjective map of sheaves. Hence (3) follows from the definition as well. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>